    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334">

                <pb facs="0455" n="1209" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/126</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received October 16.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: I beg leave
                    to acknowledge receipt of memorandum of your Department dated October 10<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d334-f1"/> transmitting a communication from Ambassador
                        Willard, in relation
                    to possible demands for the export of gold to Spain, which demands the
                    Ambassador <pb facs="0456" n="1210" xml:id="pg1210"/> thinks may be in the
                    interest of certain persons who are very close to Germany.</p>
                <p>In response permit me to say that since the embargo was placed on gold, no
                    shipments of gold to that country have been licensed, and all applications now
                    being received by the board for Spain are refused.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oscar Crosby</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
